of the new strings within the IceCube detector. The densely instrumented region (physics region) between depths of \\SIrange{2140}{2440}{m} is shown right with the positions of the acoustic pingers marked.","filename":"geometry-physics.png"}],"license":[{"url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/","license":"arXiv nonexclusive-distrib 1.0","material":"preprint"},{"license":"CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0","imposing":"SISSA"}],"texkeys":["Heinen:2019lwd"],"citeable":true,"keywords":[{"value":"detector: optical","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"detector: calibration","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"detector: acoustic","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"IceCube: upgrade","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"neutrino: energy: high","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"observatory","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"geometry","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"angular resolution","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"string","schema":"INSPIRE"}],"abstracts":[{"value":"The IceCube Neutrino Observatory will be upgraded with about 700 additional optical sensor modules and new calibration devices. Particularly, improved calibration will enhance IceCube’s physics capabilities both at low and high neutrino energies. An important ingredient for a good angular resolution of the observatory is a precise calibration of the positions of optical sensors. We present the concept of newly developed acoustic sensors that are mounted inside the optical modules and additional acoustic emitter modules that are attached to the strings. With this system we aim for the calibration of the detectors’ geometry with a precision of 10 cm by means of trilateration of the arrival times of acoustic signals. This new method will allow for an improved and complementary geometry calibration with respect to previously used methods based on optical flashers and drill logging data.","source":"SISSA"},{"value":"The IceCube Neutrino Observatory will be upgraded with about 700 additional optical sensor modules and new calibration devices. Particularly, improved calibration will enhance IceCube's physics capabilities both at low and high neutrino energies. An important ingredient for a good angular resolution of the observatory is a precise calibration of the positions of optical sensors. We present the concept of newly developed acoustic sensors that are mounted inside the optical modules and additional acoustic emitter modules that are attached to the strings. With this system we aim for the calibration of the detectors' geometry with a precision of 10\\,cm by means of trilateration of the arrival times of acoustic signals. This new method will allow for an improved and complementary geometry calibration with respect to previously used methods based on optical flashers and drill logging data.","source":"arXiv"}],"references":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1504036"},"raw_refs":[{"value":"[1] IceCube Collaboration, M. G. Aartsen et al., JINST 12 (2017) P03012.","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"misc":["IceCube Collaboration"],"label":"1","authors":[{"full_name":"Aartsen, M.G."}],"publication_info":{"year":2017,"artid":"P03012","journal_title":"JINST","journal_volume":"12"}},"curated_relation":false},{"raw_refs":[{"value":"[2] L. Peters Bachelor’s Thesis, RWTH Aachen University, 2019. in German.","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"misc":["Thesis, RWTH Aachen University,. in German"],"label":"2","authors":[{"full_name":"Bachelor's"},{"full_name":"Peters, L."}],"publication_info":{"year":2019}}},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1751107"},"raw_refs":[{"value":"[3] IceCube Collaboration, PoS(ICRC2019)1031 (these proceedings).","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"misc":["IceCube Collaboration / (these proceedings)"],"label":"3","publication_info":{"year":2019,"artid":"1031","page_start":"1031","journal_title":"PoS","journal_volume":"ICRC2019"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1751631"},"raw_refs":[{"value":"[4] IceCube Collab